{
  "requirement": "The documented coverage overview presents a compact table of source\nfiles with coverage annotations and links to their explanations.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject requires the coverage overview to present a compact table of source files that carry coverage annotations, with links to their explanations. I found no unacknowledged gap.\n\n**Table of annotated files only**\n- `src/execution_coverage/book.rs#mod[tests]/fn[documented_items_are_counted_once_with_browsable_directory_and_file_groups]` builds a fixture with annotated and unannotated files.\n- It asserts a `data-file` row for each annotated file: `code.rs`, `src/direct.rs`, `src/deep/nested.rs`, `vendor/foreign.rs` and `docs_only/deep/item.rs`.\n- It asserts there is no row for the unannotated `src/pass.rs`.\n- It checks the `<tr` opening tag of the root file row and the `</button></td><td>{count}</td>` cell layout, so the rows are real table rows.\n- It asserts the annotation counts per file and per directory, and the overall \"7 documented source items carrying coverage annotations\" summary.\n- `assert_directory_contents` and `directory_group` check that files sit in the right directory groups.\n\n**Compact**\n- The same test asserts `!html.contains(\"\\n\\n\")`.\n- It asserts absent verbose or status columns, such as `gap-percentage`, `gap-verdict` and `data-status=`.\n- That assertion is weak evidence for \"compact\", but the text sets no stricter measurable criterion.\n\n**Links to explanations**\n- For each of the three files `code.rs`, `src/direct.rs` and `src/deep/nested.rs`, the test asserts a card `href` to the note chapter. It computes that href from `notes::path` and `chapter_href`.\n- It asserts per-ordinal anchors `#coverage-note-N` in both the card and the generated \"File notes: {file}\" chapter, which also has the expected path and `File: <code>` header.\n- It asserts the explanation text, the `No tracked justification is present.` fallback, and the per-item locations such as `<code>file:line #selector</code>`.\n- It asserts that the explanation controls are collapsed by default (`aria-expanded=\"false\"` and `hidden`).\n\n**Escaping of table content**\n- `documented_paths_and_explanations_escape_html` is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It uses a path `a<&>.rs` and an explanation containing `<unsafe>`. It asserts that the HTML contains the escaped forms and not the raw `<unsafe>`.\n\nThe tests cover each obligation the text states: annotated files only, table rows, links to explanations, and a compact form.",
